      "content": "To counter the cost argument, reframe UBI not as an expense, but as a necessary structural investment preventing greater societal costs like healthcare crises, unemployment benefits, and crime. For the \"laziness\" critique, emphasize pilot program data suggesting people primarily use UBI to pursue education, start new businesses, or improve health, rather than opting out of work entirely. Conclude by arguing that the opposite—mass destitution leading to social collapse—is the far more expensive outcome.",
