    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but some people say the whole thing is just a pipe dream and that the economy would just collapse under the weight of it. they claim it's basically an impossible policy that ignores basic math and fiscal reality. do you think those people are just being regressive/stuck in the past, or is there actually a legitimate economic reason why they think it won't work?",
